invariant: INV-7
file: webpki_cfg.c
catches: webpki_session_aes
builds: bin/webpki_session_aes
reason: ch_connect takes a ch_cfg.cipher_suites list that names one suite
  twice, because the repeat check compares each entry with none before it,
  and the hello offers the server that suite twice. webpki_cfg.h holds a
  list to distinct suites, which is also what keeps it at most
  SUITE_HELD_COUNT long.

--- old
        if (cfg->cipher_suites[i] == cfg->cipher_suites[j]) {
--- new
        if (cfg->cipher_suites[i] == cfg->cipher_suites[j] && j > i) {
